<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee crop 21.74 mln bags - Specialty Assoc.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee crop 21.74 mln bags - Specialty Assoc.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop should reach 21.74 million 60-kg bags against 27 million in 1996/97, said Brazil Specialty Coffee Association (BSCA).</p>
<p>Association officials have over the past two weeks traveled more than 5,000 kilometers in key producing regions, discussing the crop outlook with producers and local traders.</p>
<p>The estimate figure was later revised at a general meeting of the BSCA, the association said in a statement.</p>
<p>A breakdown of the estimates for 1997/98 and 1996/97 by state follows. Quantities are in thousands of bags.</p>
<p>    STATE			 PRODUCTION		PRODUCTION</p>
<p>				     1997/98		    1996/97</p>
<p> PARANA				1,920			1,200</p>
<p> SAO PAULO			   2,720			3,400</p>
<p>MINAS GERAIS</p>
<p> South				 4,900			7,000</p>
<p> Cerrado			     2,280			3,800</p>
<p> Zona da Mata			2,250			3,000</p>
<p> North/west			    200			  200</p>
<p>ESPIRITO SANTO</p>
<p> Arabica			     1,350			1,800</p>
<p> Conillon			    2,700			3,600</p>
<p> BAHIA				   960			  800</p>
<p> RONDONIA			    1,260			  700</p>
<p> OTHERS				1,200			1,500</p>
<p> TOTAL				21,740		     27,000</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
</text>
